issue.description:
Polish the Workbench top-bar icon-only controls so the newly repositioned Delete theme action matches the established toolbar styling, and standardize discoverability/accessibility with shadcn tooltips.

## Goal

Make the right-side header utilities feel like one coherent control system.

This ticket has two parts:

1. normalize the Delete theme control so it uses the same visual/icon treatment as sibling top-bar icon buttons;
2. add shadcn Tooltip behavior to icon-only top-bar actions that do not have visible text labels.

## 1. Normalize Delete theme styling

The Delete theme action currently looks visually inconsistent with the surrounding top-bar icon controls.

Observed differences include:

* Delete icon appears larger than sibling toolbar icons;
* Delete does not appear to follow the same default base foreground color treatment as the rest of the header icons.

Do not hard-code a one-off size such as 14px merely to match the current screenshot.

Instead:

* inspect the existing top-bar icon-only controls such as Undo / Redo / Reset / dark-mode toggle;
* identify the accepted shared icon sizing treatment, class, wrapper, or component pattern;
* make Delete use that same sizing treatment;
* identify the accepted default foreground color treatment used by sibling controls;
* make Delete use that same default semantic foreground treatment.

The intent is system consistency, not matching a literal pixel value.

## 2. Preserve destructive semantics without making resting state inconsistent

Delete should still communicate destructive intent where interaction semantics require it.

Preferred behavior:

* resting/default icon color matches sibling top-bar controls;
* destructive styling may appear on hover, focus, pressed, or confirmation states using existing accepted patterns;
* do not make Delete permanently visually dominant in its resting state.

Preserve:

* icon-only presentation;
* current header position;
* divider placement;
* current hit target/button dimensions;
* confirmation flow;
* delete behavior;
* built-in/custom deletion rules.

## 3. Add shadcn Tooltips to icon-only top-bar controls

Standardize tooltips for top-bar controls that:

* are interactive;
* use only an icon;
* do not have a visible text label.

Audit the current right-side header utilities and apply the existing shadcn Tooltip pattern where appropriate.

Expected candidates include:

* Delete theme;
* dark/light mode toggle;
* Undo;
* Redo;
* Reset;
* any other equivalent icon-only top-bar action discovered during source inspection.

Do not add tooltips to controls that already have visible text labels such as Code or Save unless source inspection reveals a clear accessibility/discoverability need.

## 4. Tooltip copy

Keep tooltip labels concise and action-oriented.

Examples:

* Delete theme
* Toggle dark mode / Toggle light mode
* Undo
* Redo
* Reset theme

Use wording that matches the actual action semantics in the current product.

Do not introduce verbose descriptions in these tooltips.

## 5. Accessibility

Tooltips must supplement accessibility, not replace it.

Requirements:

* every icon-only control keeps or gains an appropriate accessible name;
* Tooltip text must not be the sole accessible name;
* preserve aria-label / accessible naming independently;
* keyboard focus should trigger or expose tooltip behavior according to the accepted shadcn implementation;
* disabled icon actions such as Undo/Redo must remain semantically disabled.

If the current Tooltip implementation requires a wrapper around disabled controls, use the established accessible pattern rather than breaking disabled semantics.

## 6. Use existing primitives

Reuse the existing shadcn Tooltip primitive already accepted in the project, if present.

Do not:

* add a tooltip library;
* create custom hover-only tooltip CSS;
* introduce a new icon sizing token solely for this change;
* create one-off Delete sizing/color rules if the existing toolbar treatment can be reused.

Prefer joining existing shared styles/components over duplicating them.

## 7. Preserve header behavior

Do not change:

* header height;
* top-bar ordering;
* divider structure except what is necessary to integrate shared control styling;
* dark/light mode behavior;
* undo/redo/reset semantics;
* Code behavior;
* Save behavior;
* persistence/history;
* Theme v3;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* registry;
* network/dependency boundaries.

## 8. Verification

Verify at minimum:

* Delete icon now uses the same accepted sizing treatment as sibling top-bar icon controls;
* Delete resting color uses the same accepted semantic foreground treatment as siblings;
* destructive hover/focus behavior remains appropriate;
* Delete placement/divider/confirmation behavior remain unchanged;
* all intended icon-only top-bar controls expose concise shadcn tooltips;
* tooltip copy matches actual action semantics;
* icon-only controls have independent accessible names;
* keyboard focus behavior remains correct;
* disabled Undo/Redo states remain semantically disabled and tooltip-compatible;
* controls with visible text labels are not redundantly tooltipped without reason;
* no regression to top-bar layout at narrow/wide widths.

## Acceptance

* Delete visually matches the established top-bar icon sizing and default foreground treatment through the same shared styling approach used by sibling controls.
* No static one-off pixel sizing is introduced solely for Delete when an existing shared treatment is available.
* Icon-only top-bar actions use the accepted shadcn Tooltip pattern where appropriate.
* Tooltips supplement, rather than replace, accessible names.
* Disabled-state semantics remain correct.
* Existing header layout, delete semantics, Theme v3, persistence, Design Command, mutation, registry, dependency, and network boundaries remain unchanged.
